## Permissions: viewers can search the graph and use Graph Chat
Context: The permission middleware blocks every POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE
on a domain-scoped path for the Viewer role. The Explorer's search and expand
(/dtwin/sync/filter) and Graph Chat (/dtwin/assistant/chat,
/dtwin/assistant/chat/stream) take their parameters as a POST body but only
read, so a Viewer could open the Knowledge Graph but not search it ("Viewer
role does not allow write operations").
Changes:
1. src/shared/fastapi/main.py
   New _VIEWER_READ_ONLY_POSTS: exact paths a Viewer may POST to. The viewer
   write gate skips them for POST only. Graph Chat's write actions
   (/dtwin/nodes/action/request and /confirm) stay blocked, and so does
   /dtwin/sync/load, which stays with the builder-only data-refresh
   operations.
Tests added:
- tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py (TestDomainScopedRoutes):
  viewers can POST to the three read-only paths; other /dtwin POSTs
  (sync/start, sync/load, nodes/action/request and confirm, a longer path
  with the same prefix) stay blocked; PUT, PATCH and DELETE on a read-only
  path stay blocked; a user with no team entry still cannot search.
